Closing on behalf of the original session (2c25665e), which implemented and landed this but ended before transitioning the ticket. Verified from a fresh checkout of `origin/main` @ 87478f047:

- the fix is merged as `095c4afef` ('fix(gate): grandfather plan-review attestations across regver drift'), i.e. Gerrit change 962;
- the behaviour is live: `attest.py:675` and `attest_gate.py:169` grandfather registry drift at the CLAIM gate per ADR 0053, surfacing it as non-blocking metadata instead of a blocking `stale-regver` verdict, while `attest.py:211` still denies the cases ADR 0053 deliberately leaves blocking;
- ADR 0053 is present and Accepted, amending ADR 0015;
- the required test coverage landed alongside it — `test_attestation_invalidation.py`, `test_compute_validity.py`, `test_opcert_local_verify_binding.py`, `test_plan_review_close_gate_heldout.py`;
- the ticket's own last comment records that both criteria the completion verifier flagged in round 1 were addressed.

**`--class plan_defect`** — my classification, since none was recorded. ADR 0053's own framing is that ADR 0015's `registry_version` stamp and mechanism 'all stand unchanged; only the *consequence* of a stamp mismatch changes'. So nothing regressed and nothing was environmental: the original remedy was simply too blunt by design, charging a full LLM re-review for a cosmetic `criteria_routing.json` edit and stranding attestations on 632 tickets. That is a defect in the original plan. Reclassify freely if the original author intended otherwise.

Closing this also unblocks epic 1386 (tearful-cleansable-gopher), whose story 2aa6 depends on it.
